  "message": "I fixed the header rows of both run-results tables: the single-run results table in `current.png` and the run-comparison table in `mockup.png`. The tests pass and both typechecks are clean, but I couldn't check it in a browser because the Playwright server failed to connect.\n\n**Why the labels were inconsistent**\n- **Plain column labels** (Test Case name, Total turns, HTTP, Duration, and Delta in the comparison table) had no custom header component. They fell back to the ui-kit's default grid style: 10px, uppercase, letter-spaced.\n- **Labels that did use the custom component** (`EllipsisHeader`) still inherited the kit's uppercase and letter spacing, which is why you saw \"SCORE\" and \"EXACT_MATCH\" in large capitals. \"Total requests\" was wired up a third way.\n- **Group labels** mixed the grid's default bold style (\"Execution\", \"Extracted\") with a regular-weight one (\"DeepEval: Answer Relevancy\", \"Exact Match\").\n- **Score labels on the left:** the table decided a metric column's alignment from the first row's value. When that row had no score, as with the \"\u2014\" rows in your screenshot, the label went left while the numbers sat right.\n- **Uneven spacing:** the comparison table set the group row to 28px while the other rows are 40px.\n\n**What I changed**\n- `EllipsisHeader` and `EllipsisHeaderGroup` now both use 14px semibold, normal case, no letter spacing. Group labels were regular weight before.\n- Every column and group label in both tables now uses those two components. Number columns (indexes, totals, HTTP, Duration, scores, Delta) are right-aligned; everything else is left-aligned.\n- A metric column's alignment now follows the first row that actually has a value (`src/components/Runs/View/utils.ts`).\n- I removed the 28px group-row override, so every header row is 40px. An archived design doc had added it to stop a third header row being clipped. The grid sizes its header to fit the rows, so that shouldn't happen, but it's the thing to watch when you look at it in the browser.\n- The \"INPUT BINDINGS\" group label is now \"Input bindings\", matching the other group labels. I updated its spec assertions to match.\n\nI added tests for the label style, for every column using the shared header component, and for the alignment when the first row has no score.\n\nThe two label components are also used by the comparison table's column-picker panel, so its group labels will look slightly different there. To check the change in the app, open a run's Extraction Result tab and a run comparison's Execution Results tab.",
